From: Kudbee <twd4lifez@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:50:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(server): dashboard bridge to governed upcloud-ssh
 execution (#284)

apps/web had no path to backend.main, and governed admission tokens could
only be minted in-process, so no out-of-process client could run a
governed job.

- POST /api/v1/run/admission-token (API-key authenticated) issues a 300s
  goal:execute token for a fixed server-side identity. Callers cannot
  choose agent, capability or TTL. require_http_admission is unchanged.
- apps/web/governed-bridge.ts gets the token server-side and submits to
  the existing governed POST /api/v1/run with execution_substrate fixed
  to upcloud-ssh. It forwards only an exact-match read-only command
  allow-list, requires the X-Kudbee-Client header, and fails closed
  without THINKBOX_API_KEY. The browser never sees the key or token.
- Dashboard /remote CMD terminal command.

Live: headless Chrome -> dashboard /remote hostname -> apps/web (HTTP) ->
uvicorn backend (HTTP) -> worker-02 209.50.51.174 -> "kudbee-hermes-worker-02",
exit 0, verified, with 0 console errors. Tests: f142 4/4, bridge 7/7, web
140/140, python regression 263/263. CI not run (GitHub billing issue).

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
